# ---- Compiled decks ----
# Tracked deliberately. That warning was written for the two-way Overleaf sync;
# this repo is single-author and one-way, so there is no concurrent edit to
# conflict with, and the compiled deck is what you actually want on hand when
# you open this from another machine.
# */main.pdf

# ---- Generated figures ----
# figures_src/ is the truth; figures/ is rebuilt by build_all.py.
# Uncomment if you'd rather not track the generated PDFs at all:
# class_impacts/figures/*.pdf
# class_impacts/figures/*.png

# ---- exercise/ ----
# What students clone. Two files are tracked on purpose -- the script and the
# one CSV it reads -- so that a clone runs without downloading 1.9 GB first.
# Everything the script writes is generated, and stays out.
exercise/figures/
exercise/data/derived/*
!exercise/data/derived/tmax_daily_1961_2019.csv.gz

# ---- Local only ----
# This repository is public, and it exists to hand two decks and one exercise to
# students. Everything below is real work that stays on this machine: the
# private working project, the papers and their reading notes, the house
# template, the planning documents, the parked frames, and the nine figures
# whose scripts are not published. Ignored rather than deleted -- all of it is
# still here on disk.
replication/
papers/
template/
admin/
*/OUTLINE.md
class_empirics/parked_frames.tex
class_empirics/figures/fig0*.png

.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- OS ----
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

